  ('engcbod', 'eng', 'cbod', 'Carbonaceous Biochemical Oxygen Demand', 'A measure of the amount of oxygen required by microorganisms to break down organic carbon-based compounds in water over a specified period, typically five days at 20°C (CBOD₅). Unlike BOD (Biochemical Oxygen Demand), CBOD excludes oxygen demand from the oxidation of nitrogenous compounds (such as ammonia). It is used to assess organic pollution in wastewater and natural waters.', 'NA', '3.0.0', '3.0.0', 'added in V3.0.0', NULL),
