  ('engxg', 'eng', 'xg', 'Relative Centrifugal Force (RCF) or x g units', 'RCF (Relative Centrifugal Force) denotes the degree of force exerted on a sample. RCF is quantified in multiples of the gravitational acceleration that is standard at the Earth''s surface (x g). Thus, the terms RCF and XG are often used interchangeably in centrifugation protocols.', 'NA', '2.2.0', '2.2.0', 'added in V2.2.0', NULL),
